WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.216
Zhu Yuanzhang's family was very poor; as a young man he became a monk and lived by begging for alms.

00:00:06.566 --> 00:00:10.862
Holding a worn-out bowl, Zhu Yuanzhang walked through all the nearby villages.

00:00:11.212 --> 00:00:17.740
In the Yuan dynasty's final years, Zhu Yuanzhang joined the forces resisting the Yuan, determined to change his own fate.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:23.610
Zhu Yuanzhang put on the red headscarf, and his gaze grew resolute.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:32.048
Step by step Zhu Yuanzhang built his own army and began to build a government, and more and more people came to join him.

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:39.574
Zhu Yuanzhang defeated many rivals; his power grew greater and greater, and his fame spread everywhere.

00:00:39.924 --> 00:00:46.092
Zhu Yuanzhang controlled the middle and lower reaches of the Yangtze, becoming the strongest power in the south.

00:00:46.442 --> 00:00:51.962
At sunrise, the army's fleet of boats advanced along the great river.

00:00:52.312 --> 00:00:59.752
In the end, Zhu Yuanzhang became the key figure who overthrew the Yuan dynasty, and history turned a new page.

